15 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Two sets of reliability diagrams compare predicted confidence with empirical accuracy for PlantDoc known-class evaluation before and after temperature scaling. Panel \(a\) shows Setting A, calibrated using the PlantVillage validation split; ECE decreases from 0.4771 to 0.4400. Panel \(b\) shows Setting B, calibrated using a 10% grouped PlantDoc field calibration subset; ECE decreases from 0.4761 to 0.3651. Each subplot includes a red dashed perfect-calibration diagonal and blue bars showing observed accuracy across confidence bins.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Two side-by-side coverage\205risk curve plots show the error rate among answered samples as coverage changes. Panel \(a\) shows Setting A, with thresholds selected using the PlantVillage validation split and transferred to the PlantDoc known set. Panel \(b\) shows Setting B, with thresholds selected using the grouped PlantDoc field calibration subset and applied to the held-out PlantDoc known test set. Blue curves indicate before calibration, red curves indicate after temperature scaling, and gray horizontal lines mark 5% and 10% risk levels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Boxplot graphic comparing PlantVillage and PlantDoc datasets on six measures: mean saturation, mean brightness, grayscale entropy, Laplacian variance, edge density, and foreground occupancy proxy, highlighting differences in visual characteristics between the datasets.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Grid of 16 labeled leaf images arranged in four rows and four columns. Each row shows a matched source PlantVillage image, source Grad-CAM overlay, target PlantDoc image, and target Grad-CAM overlay for the same disease category. Text labels report the true category, predicted category, confidence, and border activation ratio. In the first three rows, the model is correct on the source image but makes a high-confidence wrong prediction on the target image; the fourth row shows correct predictions with increased target border activation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Four grouped bar charts summarize the feature moment-matching baseline applied to the fine-tuned ResNet-50 under repeated grouped Setting B evaluation. The panels compare raw and calibrated outputs for accuracy, macro-F1, expected calibration error, and Brier score. Calibration reduces expected calibration error and Brier score, while accuracy and macro-F1 remain essentially unchanged because temperature scaling does not alter predicted class labels. Error bars show variability across the 10 calibration/test splits.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Four-panel plot comparing ResNet-50, ViT-S/16, and DINOv2-S/14 under repeated grouped Setting B evaluation. Panel A shows cross-domain accuracy: DINOv2-S/14 is highest at 43.2%, followed by ViT-S/16 at 41.9% and ResNet-50 at 28.0%. Panel B shows calibrated ECE, where lower is better: ViT-S/16 is lowest at 0.303, followed by DINOv2-S/14 at 0.309 and ResNet-50 at 0.331. Panel C shows unknown-detection AUROC, highest for DINOv2-S/14 at 0.764. Panel D shows selective risk at 80% coverage, lowest for DINOv2-S/14 at 52.0%.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Four-panel bar chart visualizing metrics for a warm-start end-to-end ensemble on fine-tuned ResNet-50. Top left shows accuracy_cal around 0.31; top right displays ece_cal near 0.063 with an error bar. Bottom left, predictive_confidence compares auroc_unknown and risk_at_80, both approximately 0.66. Bottom right, epistemic_confidence contrasts auroc_unknown near 0.40 with risk_at_80 near 0.67, each with small error bars.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
